			"color":"#322",
			"widgets_values":[
				"For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Top-tier Eastern xianxia VFX feature, IMAX cinematic image quality, cold cyan-blue palette, ancient wilderness at night, a sky covered by thin overcast clouds. The woman begins from the exact facial identity, pale complexion, long straight black hair, and delicate features of <Picture 1>, now reimagined as a cold ancient swordswoman suspended in the air. A medium shot orbits smoothly around her as she holds a glowing longsword in one hand and performs a sharp sword seal with the other. Her white robe and flowing sleeves flutter in the wind, while faint blue lightning gathers around her body and sword. The sword edge cuts through the air with crisp cyan trails, and her posture stays light, elegant, and razor-sharp.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the camera tilts upward and pushes in from below as she raises the longsword toward the dark sky. The sword stops at the center of the frame and becomes the eye of a huge, intricate taiji-bagua array. Blue and pink electric light expands outward in concentric rings, the outer edge of the array flickering like burning runes. The camera continues its slow push as the woman remains suspended beneath the formation, steady and unblinking, while the surrounding clouds brighten with thunder. The sword hovers motionless in the array core, and the surrounding energy grows more violent and dense.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.500, a full-body upward shot shows her directly beneath the thunder array, both arms opened wide as if drawing down the heavens. Thick lightning spears burst from the center of the formation, converging into the sword tip and then pouring over her entire body in roaring blue-white arcs. Her hair and sleeves whip in the storm, and the whole frame vibrates with overwhelming power. Lightning intensifies, the sky fractures with flashing lines, and the air around her distorts from the force.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:08.000, the camera cuts to a tight close-up pushing toward her face. Her expression is icy, calm, and utterly determined, matching the reference image’s delicate features but now filled with divine severity. She grips the sword tightly, the blade saturated with thunder until it glows almost white-blue. In one fluid motion she twists her torso and gathers momentum for a downward strike, her robes snapping around her like torn banners. Lightning crawls over her cheek, jawline, and hands, and the sword hum rises into a piercing electrical scream.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:10.500, the camera pulls back into an extreme wide shot as she slashes downward. A massive red-blue thunder pillar tears from the sword tip and轰落 onto the ancient beast below. The impact detonates into a gigantic crater, with shockwaves blasting apart ancient trees, shattered rocks, and flying debris. The beast is swallowed by the thunderstorm in a violent, high-impact visual climax. The woman remains suspended above the blast, sword still extended, while the broken sky flashes behind her and the entire battlefield is consumed by stormlight.\n\noverall_soundscape: Strong mountain wind, rolling thunder, electric crackle, sword resonance, and explosive ground impacts drive the scene. The beast’s roar is swallowed by the thunder strike, followed by collapsing debris, snapping trees, and a deep rumbling aftershock.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A high-intensity orchestral score with pounding war drums, surging strings, and metallic bass hits, building steadily into a huge thunderous climax."
